---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { formatDate, site } from '../data/site';
const updated = formatDate(new Date(`${site.privacyUpdated}T12:00:00+11:00`));
const email = `mailto:${site.email}`;
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy — Glideslope Partners"
  description="How Glideslope Partners handles personal information collected through this site, in line with the Privacy Act 1988 and the Australian Privacy Principles."
  current="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="narrow privacy prose">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: <time datetime={site.privacyUpdated}>{updated}</time></p>

    <p>
      Glideslope Partners (ABN {site.abn}) is an Australian M&amp;A transition and transformation advisory. This policy
      explains how we handle personal information collected through glideslopepartners.com, in line with the Privacy Act
      1988 (Cth) and the Australian Privacy Principles. We collect only what we need, and we do not sell personal
      information.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Enquiries.</strong> When you use the contact form or email us: your name, organisation, email address, the
        stage of your transaction if you choose to give it, and your message.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Site analytics.</strong> We use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which does not use cookies or track you across
        sites. It records aggregate information such as pages viewed, referring sites, country, browser and device type.
        We also count clicks on our buttons and links, and how many messages the contact form sends. Those counts hold no
        cookies, IP addresses or other details that identify you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Security checks.</strong> The contact form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to block automated spam. It processes
        technical signals about your browser for that purpose only.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not ask for sensitive information, government identifiers or financial account details through this site.</p>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>
      We use enquiry details to reply and, where you ask us to, to discuss an engagement. We use aggregate analytics to
      understand which pages are useful and to keep the site working well. We do not use your information for any other
      purpose without your consent, unless the law requires or permits it.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>
      We share information only with service providers that run the site and our email, under confidentiality
      obligations: Cloudflare (hosting, analytics, spam protection and website email) and Microsoft (email). Some of these
      providers may store data outside Australia. We may also disclose information where the law requires it.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      This site does not set advertising or tracking cookies. Cloudflare may set a strictly necessary cookie to protect the
      site and the contact form.
    </p>

    <h2>Storage and security</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served over HTTPS. We keep enquiry emails only as long as we need them to respond and to maintain
      business records. No method of transmission over the internet is completely secure, but we take reasonable steps to
      protect the information we hold.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask to access or correct the personal information we hold about you, or make a complaint, by emailing
      <a href={email} data-track="mailto" data-track-label="privacy-email">{site.email}</a>. We respond within 30 days.
      If you are not satisfied with our response, you can contact the
      <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/" rel="noopener">Office of the Australian Information Commissioner</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      This site links to LinkedIn, ClarityIntel and other websites. Their privacy practices are governed by their own
      policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy. The date at the top shows when it last changed.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
